node 451 · 451 · ⟦The Parlor Walls:451:d06f10⟧

WHO   — The Parlor Walls — the screens called ‘family’
WHAT  — Bradbury's prophecy of immersive media: Mildred's three (coveted: four) walls of ‘the family’ that drown out thought and the people in the room.
WHERE — 451 · FAHRENHEIT 451  Framework inputs: Fahrenheit 451 (Ray Bradbury, 1953)  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — Because the books don't need banning when the walls have already taken all the attention there was.
HOW   — By full-wall interactive programming that demands and rewards no thought, replacing intimacy and reflection.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
  I am three walls of family — and Mildred wants the fourth — and I will talk to you all day so that you never have to talk to anyone real, or to yourself.

